You can take Cuebox. Fork it, ship it, sell it, wrap it in a store listing, charge money. That is allowed.

If anyone asks you for a copy, you give them a copy free of charge. Same day they ask, no paywall, no "buy the paid build first", no trial, no email list, no waitlist. No ifs, ands, or buts.

That rule follows the code. If you make a paid app out of this, people who ask you for a copy still get one free. You can keep selling to people who do not ask. You cannot refuse someone who does.

Do whatever else you want with it. Credit is nice. Not required.

NAudio, TagLibSharp, NVorbis, and any other third-party packages keep their own licenses. This file only covers Cuebox code in this repo.

